!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section N2O: N2O + hv --> N2 + O(1D)
! source : JPL-2006
! http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295
! -> Catalogue -> " Nitrogen oxides" -> "Nitrous oxide N2O" -> "JPL-2006"
! Rem1: Quantum yield = 1.
! Rem2: Temperature influence:   
!   i)  160-174nm: JPL-2006 reports values without mentioning the temperature influence.
!       They are not used here **** BUT SHOULD BE !!
!   ii) 174-240nm: T dep. according to the formula:
!           ln crs = sum An*wl^n + (T-300)*exp (sum Bn*wl^n)
!       where An and Bn are parameters introduced in CRS_TDEP.
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP.
!       Accordingly, the values provided below are for T=298K and ARE NOT USED !!
! Rem3: JPL-2011 (tables 4C-8 and 4C-9, p.4C-43) keeps the same values and T dependence
!       as JPL-2006 **** BUT ALSO MENTIONS A VALUE OF 2.5e-17 AT LYMAN_ALPHA !!!
!       reporting measurements at 298K in 6.1-168nm by Chan et al. (Chem. Phys., 180, 77-88, 1994)
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        45  | Finishes at wl interval :   75
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!  no  from(nm) to(nm)  | crs (cm2) | qyield (0->1) |   Tdep_param1 |   Tdep_param2
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
